== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [Which of these is an allotrope of sulphur?], [white phosphorus], [monoclinic sulphur], [graphite], [ozone])

#mcq(2, [A soap molecule removes grease because its tail], [dissolves in water], [is ionic], [is basic], [dissolves in the grease while the head stays in the water])

#mcq(3, [Which of these is a property of a typical alloy rather than of the pure metal?], [lower melting point and greater hardness], [higher melting point and greater softness], [greater electrical conductivity], [greater chemical reactivity])

#mcq(4, [On strong heating, potassium nitrate gives], [potassium oxide and nitrogen dioxide], [potassium and nitrogen], [potassium nitrite and oxygen], [potassium peroxide and oxygen])

#mcq(5, [Where is stainless steel used rather than mild steel?], [in car body panels], [in railway track], [in cutlery and chemical plant], [in structural beams])

#mcq(6, [The gas that gives a pop with a lighted splint is], [oxygen], [ammonia], [chlorine], [hydrogen])

#mcq(7, [The bond in hydrogen chloride is], [a polar covalent bond], [a purely ionic bond], [a metallic bond], [a non-polar covalent bond])

#mcq(8, [Hard water wastes soap because the calcium ions], [make the soap alkaline], [precipitate the soap as scum], [dissolve the soap], [neutralise the soap])

#mcq(9, [Which of these is NOT a property of transition metals such as iron and copper?], [they form coloured compounds], [they are all found native], [they act as catalysts], [they have variable oxidation states])

#mcq(10, [When a piece of calcium is added to water, the solution becomes milky if], [the calcium is impure], [hydrogen is not evolved], [the water is cold and the hydroxide is only slightly soluble], [the calcium is heated first])

#mcq(11, [Aluminium hydroxide is precipitated from sodium aluminate by], [adding acid], [electrolysis], [adding cryolite], [cooling and seeding the solution])

#mcq(12, [The industrial separation of nitrogen from air depends on], [their different boiling points], [their different colours], [their different densities at room temperature], [their reaction with water])

#mcq(13, [Which of these is NOT a use of sulphuric acid?], [the manufacture of fertilisers], [the lead–acid accumulator], [the bleaching of cotton by oxidation], [the manufacture of detergents])

#mcq(14, [Pyrex-type glass contains], [lead oxide], [iron(III) oxide], [cobalt oxide], [boron oxide])

#mcq(15, [The series of metals arranged in order of decreasing reactivity is called the], [reactivity series], [periodic table], [electrochemical cell], [activity coefficient])

#mcq(16, [Magnesium is used in flares because it], [is cheap], [burns with a brilliant white light], [is a good conductor], [melts easily])

#mcq(17, [Which type of steel would be chosen for a car body panel?], [high-carbon steel], [mild steel], [cast iron], [stainless steel])

#mcq(18, [In the Ostwald process, the absorption of nitrogen dioxide in water gives], [ammonia], [nitrous acid only], [nitric acid], [nitrogen])

#mcq(19, [The reaction of sulphur with iron filings gives], [iron(II) sulphide], [iron(III) sulphide], [iron(II) sulphate], [iron and hydrogen sulphide])

#mcq(20, [A water sample contains 16.2 mg of calcium hydrogencarbonate in 1.00 kg of water. Its hardness expressed as calcium carbonate is about], [16 ppm], [100 ppm], [162 ppm], [10 ppm])

#mcq(21, [Bauxite is purified before it is electrolysed because], [the ore is radioactive], [the impurities would contaminate the aluminium produced], [cryolite reacts with alumina], [the purification produces hydrogen])

#mcq(22, [The thermal decomposition of magnesium carbonate gives], [magnesium oxide and carbon dioxide], [magnesium hydroxide and carbon dioxide], [magnesium and oxygen], [magnesium oxide and carbon])

#mcq(23, [The metal produced in the Hall–Héroult cell collects], [at the top of the electrolyte], [on the anodes], [in the gas outlet], [at the bottom of the cell])

#mcq(24, [The number of moles of ammonia in 4.48 dm³ of the gas at s.t.p. is], [0.10 mol], [0.50 mol], [0.20 mol], [1.00 mol])

#mcq(25, [Concentrated sulphuric acid conducts electricity poorly because], [it contains no ions at all], [it is only slightly ionised], [it is a metal], [it has a high boiling point])

#mcq(26, [Scaling in a boiler is a problem because the scale], [is a good conductor], [dissolves in water], [is a poor conductor of heat and wastes fuel], [is lighter than water])

#mcq(27, [Which method protects iron by making use of a more reactive metal?], [painting], [electroplating with tin], [alloying with chromium], [galvanising])

#mcq(28, [The alkali metals have low densities. This means that], [they float on water], [they sink in water], [they are gases], [they dissolve in oil])

#mcq(29, [Which reaction in the blast furnace is endothermic?], [CO₂ + C → 2CO], [C + O₂ → CO₂], [CaO + SiO₂ → CaSiO₃], [Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂])

#mcq(30, [The gas that extinguishes a burning splint and turns limewater milky is], [oxygen], [nitrogen], [hydrogen], [carbon dioxide])

#mcq(31, [Which of these would you use to distinguish chlorine from hydrogen chloride?], [a lighted splint], [damp blue litmus paper, which chlorine bleaches], [limewater], [barium chloride solution])

#mcq(32, [The mass of washing soda needed to soften water containing 0.10 mol of calcium ions is], [5.3 g], [21.2 g], [10.6 g], [106 g])

#mcq(33, [Which pair of metals would both react with dilute sulphuric acid to give hydrogen?], [copper and silver], [gold and platinum], [magnesium and zinc], [lead and copper])

#mcq(34, [Which of these is the correct formula of the hydroxide of barium?], [BaOH], [Ba(OH)₂], [Ba₂OH], [BaH₂])

#mcq(35, [Which of these will dissolve in both hydrochloric acid and sodium hydroxide solution?], [aluminium], [iron], [copper], [gold])

#mcq(36, [The mass of 11.2 dm³ of ammonia at s.t.p. is], [17 g], [22.4 g], [34 g], [8.5 g])

#mcq(37, [Chlorine water is used as a bleach and a disinfectant because it contains], [hypochlorous acid], [hydrochloric acid only], [hydrogen], [sodium chloride])

#mcq(38, [The glycerol formed in saponification is used in], [cement], [glass], [cosmetics and explosives], [fertiliser])

#mcq(39, [The reaction 2K + 2H₂O → 2KOH + H₂ shows that potassium is], [less reactive than hydrogen], [more reactive than hydrogen], [a transition metal], [unreactive with water])

#mcq(40, [Which of these is the correct equation for the reaction of calcium with water?], [Ca + H₂O → CaO + H₂], [Ca + 2H₂O → CaH₂ + O₂], [2Ca + H₂O → Ca₂O + H₂], [Ca + 2H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ + H₂])

